{
  "name": "Email document intake: OCR, classify, file to Drive, and index every attachment",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Email document intake: OCR, classify, file to Drive, and index every attachment\n\n**Community node.** This template uses the pdfRest API Toolkit community node (@pdfrest/n8n-nodes-pdfrest), so it runs on self-hosted n8n only. Install it under Settings > Community Nodes before importing.\n\n### Who it's for\n\nTeams whose inbox is a document intake channel: accounts payable, legal ops, property management, anyone who receives invoices, contracts, and signed forms by email and files them by hand.\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow monitors Gmail for incoming messages, splits each attachment into its own item, and standardizes the binary data for processing. It checks PDF metadata, applies OCR when needed, converts the document to markdown, and uses an AI-powered Information Extractor (Anthropic Claude shown; any chat model works) to classify the document. Based on the classification, it files the attachment into the correct Google Drive folder, appends an index row in Google Sheets, and sends a Slack notification.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect and authorize the Gmail trigger for the mailbox or label that receives document intake emails.\n- Configure the folder IDs, index Sheet ID, Slack channel ID (right-click the channel in Slack > View channel details), and OCR languages in the Set Folder and Index IDs node.\n- Add a pdfRest API credential (API key from pdfrest.com) for the three pdfRest nodes and confirm the expected binary property is `data`.\n- Connect an Anthropic credential to the Anthropic Chat Model subnode (or swap in OpenAI, Gemini, or a local model) and verify the Document Type Classifier output matches the Route by Document Type switch rules.\n- Authorize Google Drive and Google Sheets credentials, then select the destination Drive folders and the spreadsheet used as the document index.\n- Authorize Slack credentials and configure the target channel or user for completion notifications.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the document categories, folder mappings, classification prompt/schema, index columns, and Slack message content to match your filing taxonomy. To add a document type: add it to the attribute description in Document Type Classifier, add a rule in Route by Document Type, add a Prepare node for it, and a folder ID in Set Folder and Index IDs. For records retention, add pdfRest's Convert \u00b7 PDF to PDF/A (Archival) after Apply OCR to PDF. Swap Slack for Microsoft Teams or email, or narrow the Gmail filter to a label for a single-purpose inbox.",
        "height": 1120,
        "width": 480
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        128,
        224
      ],
      "id": "7c86c094-6fc8-4384-8ac3-394913de8f24",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
